# The eight principles

Scope: the why behind the practice — the eight information-architecture principles as a concept facet. Explanation mode. Consult a principle for rationale; each links to the how-to that applies it and the reference it draws on.

These principles are one path into the skill, not its file hierarchy. The hierarchy is by mode (`explanation/` / `how-to/` / `reference/`) and the primary routing is by job and trigger (`../../SKILL.md`). Read a principle here when you want to understand *why* a move is right; act on it via the linked how-to.

| Principle | Concept page | Applied by |
|---|---|---|
| 1. Organize around user intent | `01-organize-around-user-intent.md` | `../../how-to/design-around-intent.md` |
| 2. Typed, source-of-truth topics | `02-typed-source-of-truth-topics.md` | `../../how-to/type-a-topic.md` |
| 3. Hubs as orientation and routing | `03-hubs-orientation-and-routing.md` | `../../how-to/build-hubs.md` |
| 4. Multiple paths to a topic | `04-multiple-paths.md` | `../../how-to/add-paths.md` |
| 5. Controlled vocabulary and metadata | `05-controlled-vocabulary-and-metadata.md` | `../../how-to/set-vocabulary-and-metadata.md` |
| 6. Information scent at every click | `06-information-scent.md` | `../../how-to/strengthen-scent.md` |
| 7. Nonlinear information seeking | `07-nonlinear-information-seeking.md` | `../../how-to/support-nonlinear-seeking.md` |
| 8. Validate and iterate | `08-validate-and-iterate.md` | `../../how-to/validate.md`, `../../how-to/govern.md` |

The principles compose: intent (1) decides what to build; typing (2) and hubs (3) and paths (4) build it; vocabulary (5), scent (6), and nonlinear design (7) make it findable; validation (8) keeps it honest.

Related: the distinctions and dimensions these assume `../foundations.md`; the loop that runs them `../../how-to/procedure.md`.
